{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"39","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. C*++ Calculations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"64 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C*++ language is quite similar to C++. The similarity manifests itself in the fact that the programs written in C*++ sometimes behave unpredictably and lead to absolutely unexpected effects. For example, let's imagine an arithmetic expression in C*++ that looks like this ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"expression"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the main term):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"expression"},{"kind":"text","text":" ::= "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"summand"},{"kind":"text","text":" | "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"expression + summand"},{"kind":"text","text":" | "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"expression - summand"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"summand"},{"kind":"text","text":" ::= "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"increment"},{"kind":"text","text":" | "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"coefficient"},{"kind":"text","text":"*"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"increment"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"increment"},{"kind":"text","text":" ::= a++ | ++a "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"coefficient"},{"kind":"text","text":" ::= 0|1|2|...|1000 "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5*a++-3*++a+a++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is a valid expression in C*++."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, we have a sum consisting of several summands divided by signs \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Every summand is an expression \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"++a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" multiplied by some integer coefficient. If the coefficient is omitted, it is suggested being equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The calculation of such sum in C*++ goes the following way. First all the summands are calculated one after another, then they are summed by the usual arithmetic rules. If the summand contains \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then during the calculation first the value of the \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" variable is multiplied by the coefficient, then value of \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is increased by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the summand contains \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"++a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then the actions on it are performed in the reverse order: first \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is increased by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", then — multiplied by the coefficient."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The summands may be calculated in any order, that's why sometimes the result of the calculation is completely unpredictable! Your task is to find its largest possible value."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first input line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 1000 ≤ a ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the initial value of the variable \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". The next line contains an expression in C*++ language of the described type. The number of the summands in the expression does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1000"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that the line describing the expression contains no spaces and tabulation. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single number — the maximal possible value of the expression."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n5*a++-3*++a+a++\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"11\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\na+++++a\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the second example. Initially "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":". Suppose that at first the first summand is calculated, and then the second one is. The first summand gets equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the value of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is increased by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". At the calculation of the second summand "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is increased once more (gets equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The value of the second summand is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"5"},{"kind":"text","text":", and together they give "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"8"},{"kind":"text","text":". If we calculate the second summand first and the first summand later, then the both summands equals to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the result is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"8"},{"kind":"text","text":", too."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"39A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/39/problem/A"}